  "raw_response": "```python\ndef solve(grid):\n    if not grid:\n        return []\n    R = len(grid)\n    C = len(grid[0])\n    \n    # Locate all 2s and 3s\n    twos_pos = []\n    threes_pos = []\n    for r in range(R):\n        for c in range(C):\n            v = grid[r][c]\n            if v == 2:\n                twos_pos.append((r, c))\n            elif v == 3:\n                threes_pos.append((r, c))\n    \n    if not twos_pos or not threes_pos:\n        return [row[:] for row in grid]\n    \n    # Determine orientation of the 2-line\n    rows_2 = [r for r, c in twos_pos]\n    cols_2 = [c for r, c in twos_pos]\n    \n    if len(set(rows_2)) == 1:\n        # Horizontal line of 2s\n        orient = 'h'\n        line_pos = rows_2[0]  # the row\n        span_start = min(cols_2)\n        span_stop = max(cols_2)\n    else:\n        # Vertical line of 2s\n        orient = 'v'\n        line_pos = cols_2[0]  # the column\n        span_start = min(rows_2)\n        span_stop = max(rows_2)\n    \n    # Bounding box of 3s\n    rows_3 = [r for r, c in threes_pos]\n    cols_3 = [c for r, c in threes_pos]\n    min_r3, max_r3 = min(rows_3), max(rows_3)\n    min_c3, max_c3 = min(cols_3), max(cols_3)\n    \n    dr = 0\n    dc = 0\n    eight_cells = []\n    \n    if orient == 'v':\n        # Vertical barrier\n        if min_c3 > line_pos:\n            # 3s are to the right, move left to touch\n            new_min_c = line_pos + 1\n            dc = new_min_c - min_c3\n            new_max_c = max_c3 + dc\n            # Place 8s on the far side (right) of the moved 3s\n            eight_c = new_max_c + 1\n            for r in range(span_start, span_stop + 1):\n                eight_cells.append((r, eight_c))\n        else:\n            # 3s are to the left, move right to touch\n            new_max_c = line_pos - 1\n            dc = new_max_c - max_c3\n            new_min_c = min_c3 + dc\n            # Place 8s on the far side (left) of the moved 3s\n            eight_c = new_min_c - 1\n            for r in range(span_start, span_stop + 1):\n                eight_cells.append((r, eight_c))\n    else:\n        # Horizontal barrier\n        if min_r3 > line_pos:\n            # 3s are below, move up to touch\n            new_min_r = line_pos + 1\n            dr = new_min_r - min_r3\n            new_max_r = max_r3 + dr\n            # Place 8s on the far side (below) of the moved 3s\n            eight_r = new_max_r + 1\n            for c in range(span_start, span_stop + 1):\n                eight_cells.append((eight_r, c))\n        else:\n            # 3s are above, move down to touch\n            new_max_r = line_pos - 1\n            dr = new_max_r - max_r3\n            new_min_r = min_r3 + dr\n            # Place 8s on the far side (above) of the moved 3s\n            eight_r = new_min_r - 1\n            for c in range(span_start, span_stop + 1):\n                eight_cells.append((eight_r, c))\n    \n    # Construct output\n    out = [row[:] for row in grid]\n    \n    # Erase original 3s\n    for r, c in threes_pos:\n        out[r][c] = 0\n    \n    # Draw moved 3s\n    for r, c in threes_pos:\n        nr, nc = r + dr, c + dc\n        if 0 <= nr < R and 0 <= nc < C:\n            out[nr][nc] = 3\n    \n    # Draw 8s\n    for r, c in eight_cells:\n        if 0 <= r < R and 0 <= c < C:\n            out[r][c] = 8\n    \n    return out\n```",
